        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                "word": "altérité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0e97195a-29b2-45ac-ab9e-1a6d6579db01",
                        "entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "altérités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                        "entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fait d’être autre, d’être distinct."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "22d77c0a-b6c8-40a7-a7be-ac055b536a90",
                                "sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                                "text": "Ce que M. Mannoni a oublié, c’est que le Malgache n’existe plus ; il a oublié que le Malgache existe avec l’Européen. Le Blanc arrivant à Madagascar a bouleversé les horizons et les mécanismes psychologiques. Tout le monde l’a dit, l’altérité pour le Noir, ce n’est pas le Noir, mais le Blanc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf914149-1070-40ed-bcf5-7679615b3fc3",
                                "sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                                "text": "Lorsque j’écris, je fais l’expérience d’une altérité. Je suis autant scribe qui écoute qu’écrivain qui crée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3a2af7d-1f7d-427d-80c3-3b1c0b766466",
                                "sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                                "text": "Connaître en droit et connaître en fait, c’est du pareil au même puisqu’entre deux, nulle altérité n’a le droit de s’immiscer. Le droit fait comme s’il était le fait."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a700f8a8-c504-4d00-82bf-322bedf2ca7e",
                                "sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                                "text": "La société médiévale est, par rapport à nous, objectivement, une société radicalement autre. Mais l’appréhension de cette altérité est entravée par deux processus, certes opposés (…) mais qui aboutissent au même résultat – l’incompréhension."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f056f25e-d5bf-4ed2-b861-7abf8b941fdd",
                                "sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                                "text": "Les parents ont tendances à beaucoup projeter sur leurs enfants, à en faire leur miroir. Le risque c’est que leur altérité et leur personnalité ne soient respectées."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "df2f2d63-b2ae-420a-a5db-8cdb881c234c",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                        "target_lang_word": "Anderssein",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "809e7880-0d44-41bd-8366-d04707462dcc",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                        "target_lang_word": "Andersartigkeit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Andersartigkeit",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74e5fda3-3205-3935-838f-2a45cc1773a8",
                                        "entry_id": "490ccd22-6914-3a81-bdb6-a712f259e5ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Eigenschaft, sich in irgendeiner Weise grundsätzlich von anderen/etwas anderem zu unterscheiden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a120ebf-8cac-4ec1-927c-91d5b38bc9a3",
                                                "sense_id": "74e5fda3-3205-3935-838f-2a45cc1773a8",
                                                "text": "„Warum wir andersartig waren und warum es wichtig war, diese Andersartigkeit zu bewahren, das haben mir meine Eltern nie wirklich erklärt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f29f5a6-4d0f-4360-8145-7894440cd438",
                                                "sense_id": "74e5fda3-3205-3935-838f-2a45cc1773a8",
                                                "text": "„Die große Andersartigkeit Afghanistans gibt dem Westen Rätsel auf.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29f1e20b-0662-4d4f-9d53-2849ec6fc03f",
                                                "sense_id": "74e5fda3-3205-3935-838f-2a45cc1773a8",
                                                "text": "„Aber vielleicht passte die deutsche Bedeutung besser, denn fremd war nicht genug, um die Andersartigkeit der Kreatur vor uns auszudrücken, dieser riesigen orangefarbenen Augen mit einem unbekannten Bewusstsein dahinter.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d71a2f52-1516-436a-a094-979d65f3e563",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                        "target_lang_word": "otherness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "otherness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2541d57a-f769-38e0-9062-a41ecf11c9d9",
                                        "entry_id": "ff687ad6-5eb8-3cb1-9c1e-d2a14bbb10a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being different or distinct."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2925fd04-72e6-412c-83ca-08f4e697d5b7",
                                                "sense_id": "2541d57a-f769-38e0-9062-a41ecf11c9d9",
                                                "text": "As Floya Anthias argues in her chapter, there is a need to fight against all those constructions of difference and identity that exclude and devalorise, and against all those social practices that construct identities and differences in naturalised, collectivised and binary ways and in terms of hierarchical otherness, unequal resource allocation and modes of inferiorisation (see also Anthias 1998a)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "adf4b88f-2996-3b7c-8de8-8545e1afe0ac",
                                        "entry_id": "ff687ad6-5eb8-3cb1-9c1e-d2a14bbb10a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The result or product of being different or distinct."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b5f152fa-6845-4ea7-9629-ffc0600129ae",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5d76230-d3a1-3611-88e1-b977e0a27242",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1032a60-ff25-3896-8485-d850a4abed75",
                        "target_lang_word": "alterity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alterity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80146535-5b4a-31fe-9874-8f5168ad4428",
                                        "entry_id": "c648c7bf-dd76-3d11-bab1-096bf06f1a36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Otherness; the entity in contrast to which an identity is constructed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1644446-cf80-4b1c-950b-df5bb0fc8cf8",
                                                "sense_id": "80146535-5b4a-31fe-9874-8f5168ad4428",
                                                "text": "Nominal declensions, verbal case endings, gerundival constructions, in short, the full range of grammatical alterations—for which Sanskrit has a particular genius and meticulous order—announce language itself as a field of alterity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
